  "message": "When the Lance DB table that holds our shared‑memory gets compacted, everything that’s been saved there—notes, context, any facts we’ve stored—gets cleared. The language model itself isn’t altered; it just starts with a clean slate the next time it runs, so we lose the conversation history that was in the database.\n\nRight now there isn’t another LLM silently reading all of that data, summarizing it and writing the summary back while deleting the raw entries. The compaction is a blunt “clear everything” operation, not a selective summar‑and‑keep process.\n\nIf you’d like a more intelligent approach—having an LLM scan the stored facts, produce a concise summary, store that summary, and then wipe the detailed entries—we’d need to build a new helper for it. I can set up a custom agent that does exactly that whenever you ask. Let me know if you want to create one.",
